<p>I like the idea, but this could use some work.</p>
<p>The tests seem somewhat limited. First of all, I <em>believe</em> that you can defeat one way mirrors by placing an extremely bright light in contact with the glass. Google is failing me, but I remember reading somewhere that it basically lights up the room on the other side enough to see into the other area.</p>
<p>Second, <a href="http://http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laser_microphone">this</a> technology can be used to listen to sounds on the other side of a window by reading the vibrations of the glass. Has this been tried?</p>
<p>Third, what about low-light cameras and image enhancement software? Do they show up on camera?</p>
<p>Finally, on a stylistic note, and this should be taken with a huge chunk of salt, maybe have the test logs end and pick up with a personal diary?</p>

