														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1546447">
									

<p>The light source thing I'll readily concede, it was something I read long ago <em>somewhere</em>. Although going by the description, it seems that it still might work, and &quot;no result&quot; would still tell the foundation something.</p>
<p>The laser microphone, done right, could be another method to scare the bejeezus out of us - maybe even an audio log? Even if there's no speech, the ambient audio in the viewing chamber could be incredibly creepy.</p>
<p>&nbsp;I'd accept &quot;low-light cameras revealed no additional information.&quot; as an answer for that test as well.</p>
<p>The Foundation is meticulous and has huge resources, visual observation is where they'd start, not stop.</p>
<p>In addition, the article suffers from a dearth of details, things the researchers would be able to tell even from visual observation:</p>
<p>What are they writing in? Notebooks? Bibles? Ledgers? Clipboards? [REDACTED]?</p>
<p>How big are they? If they're smoking a known brand of cigarette, they'd probably be able extrapolate from there.</p>
<p>Are they fat? Thin? Talk? Short?</p>
<p>Do they have distinguishing characteristics - can you tell one individual from another? Are their suits identical?</p>
<p>Are they watching the mirror like a window, or a TV screen? In other words, do they sit still and watch, or do they bend to see things from a different angle?</p>
<p>These are just off the top of my head. I really like the concept here, but the article needs work.</p>

