<p>I like the direction youre going here, and I'm going to give you a tenuous upvote for encouragement. I want to reiterate, I find this concept to be freaky as hell, and I paid a bit more attention to the mirrors I came across in my life last night. :)</p>
<p>That being said, I think it still needs a lot of work on tone and cohesion. I should have access to a PC (posting from my ipod) after Sunday, I could do a bit of polishing to show you what I mean then (posting it here, not in the main article) if you'd like.</p>
<p>As for the &quot;recognizing individual watchers&quot; concept, I brought it up because played right it could add to the freak factor: noticing that test subjects start being studied by &quot;their&quot; watcher - almost turning it from observation to a stalking.</p>
<p>Also, and I'd be willing to try my hand at this as well if you'd like, by audio log, I was thinking of an <em>actual</em> audio log - an embedded MP3 file or maybe even a YouTube video (You could show an oscilloscope or perhaps a still of a bathroom mirror with the glow of a lit cigarette barely visible. I'm not bad at doing stuff like that, so if you'd like that, I'm willing to help.</p>
<p>Keep up the good work!</p>

